Defines five error types for the steno compiler pipeline, each wrapping a human-readable message; all four `*Error` types implement `std::error::Error` and `Display`.

`StrokeError` surfaces from stroke parsing, rendering, merging, or count-bank arithmetic. `StenoError` wraps parse failures and carries the 1-based source line; call `line()` to retrieve it. `ExpandError` is emitted by count- and type-expansion passes and collects errors from downstream: `StrokeError`, `RenderError`, and `SnippetError` all convert to `ExpandError` via `From`, preserving the message but discarding source context. `RenderError` indicates an unresolved chunk reached a renderer or a movement target is not up-and-left of the resting cursor. `SnippetError` indicates an unresolved chunk reached the snippet renderer. All errors are opaque strings — no structured variants or context fields beyond line numbers.